CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main.assertion.\d+\] .* assertion y == 1: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
This test checks that the loop assigns inference does not consider calls to
functions that DFCC does not instrument (here, with the `__VERIFIER` prefix).
Such a call made the may-alias analysis treat every pointer whose address is
taken as unknown, so that `*p` aliased `y`, `y` was havocked, and the assertion
failed.
